{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1411762-level-6-caern","id":1411762,"title":"Level 6 Caern?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-04T01:57:44-07:00","id":1411762,"title":"Level 6 Caern?","content":"AFAIK there is no rule about Level 6 Caern. The only one I know is the Pangea\u2019s Graveyard of the Lost in Umbra Revised (Level 5 in W20 version, though)<br /> <br /> If, I say if, such great caern does exist, how should it like? How can you CREATE one like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T21:06:34-07:00","id":1411998,"title":"","content":"No way, in the modern era. It would have to be a unique plot device that would mark the ending/ birth of an age. If it existed there would have to be a unique story behind it, something along the lines of Gaia giving her chosen a place to make a last stand, the result of an epic quest that saved Gaia and healed the Wyrm, or maybe something that was dormant since the time before the Wyrm went mad, and Gaia preserves within herself for the fated moment that would decide everything. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, it could be a Mokole secret that is connected to the Dragon Kings, or the result of some Mage experimenting on a captured or discovered Caern and accidentally improving it in some way that it was not meant to be altered. Maybe empowering a Caern to level 6 is actually a bad thing and it is hurting Gaia by creating some sort of imbalance on her body.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is related to Final Fantasy: the Spirits Within, and the Level 6 Caern is actually the last, spiritual remains of an alien Gaia that crashed on to Earth and partially merged with our Gaia. <br /> <br /> Lastly, the size and shape could be anything since a Level 6 Caern is breaking all of the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-05-2020, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T03:21:08-07:00","id":1412036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1411762-level-6-caern?p=1411998#post1411998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No way, in the modern era. It would have to be a unique plot device that would mark the ending/ birth of an age. If it existed there would have to be a unique story behind it, something along the lines of Gaia giving her chosen a place to make a last stand, the result of an epic quest that saved Gaia and healed the Wyrm, or maybe something that was dormant since the time before the Wyrm went mad, and Gaia preserves within herself for the fated moment that would decide everything.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it could be a Mokole secret that is connected to the Dragon Kings, or the result of some Mage experimenting on a captured or discovered Caern and accidentally improving it in some way that it was not meant to be altered. Maybe empowering a Caern to level 6 is actually a bad thing and it is hurting Gaia by creating some sort of imbalance on her body.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is related to Final Fantasy: the Spirits Within, and the Level 6 Caern is actually the last, spiritual remains of an alien Gaia that crashed on to Earth and partially merged with our Gaia.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the size and shape could be anything since a Level 6 Caern is breaking all of the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always think this Graveyard is just a passing fancy of authority, who wanted to represent how badass is it. To be honest I dislike it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}